The '''Lothal City Capitol Building''', also known as the '''Republic Senate Building''' or '''Lothal Senate Building''', was a government building in [[Capital City]] on the [[planet]] [[Lothal]] that was built during the [[time]] of the [[Galactic Republic]]. Following the [[Proclamation of the New Order|rise]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], it was abandoned in favor of the new [[Imperial Complex (Lothal)|Imperial Complex]] and became known as the '''Old Republic Senate Building'''. However, it remained standing despite the new government's intention to raze it. The building came alive once more following the fifteenth [[Empire Day|anniversary]] of the Empire, as the meeting site between the the [[Spectres|rebel crew]] of the ''[[Ghost]]'' and [[Senator]] [[Gall Trayvis]].

==Layout==
A distinct landmark of [[Capital City]],<ref name="Lothal Old Republic Senate Building" /> the [[Lothal]] [[City]] [[Capital|Capitol]] Building,<ref name="Concept Art Gallery">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/vision-of-hope-concept-art-gallery|text="Vision of Hope" Concept Art Gallery}} {{C|Slides 6, 10, 11, 12, and 13}}</ref> also known as the Republic Senate Building<ref name="Imperial Justice">''[[Servants of the Empire: Imperial Justice]]''</ref> or Lothal Senate Building,<ref name="Trivia Gallery" /> was shaped like a round box crowned by a towering spire.<ref name="Vision of Hope">{{Rebels|Vision of Hope}}</ref> Like most other buildings in the [[city]],<ref name="SW:R:TVG">''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> its outer walls were predominantly white. Several [[starship]] landing pads sprouting from the base of the tower led to hallways hooking up with the senate chamber inside the building. The Chamber itself contained a podium with a speakers' stand, facing two aisles made of three rows of seatings.<ref name="Vision of Hope" /> On the back wall behind the podium was "[[New Freedom]]," a striking mural that contributed to the building's fame.<ref name="Lothal Old Republic Senate Building" /> The Senate Building was directly linked to the sewers of Capital City.<ref name="Vision of Hope" /> Statues stood outside the capitol building that supposedly personifyed freedom, perseverance, or the pioneer spirit.<ref name="Imperial Justice" />

==History==
During the [[time]] of the [[Galactic Republic]], the Lothal City Capitol Building of Capital City housed the [[Lothal Senate|governing body]] of Lothal. It was abandoned when the [[Galactic Empire]] replaced the Republic and built the [[Imperial Complex (Lothal)|Imperial Complex]] to be the new seat of power on the planet, becoming known as the Old Republic Senate Building.<ref name="Lothal Old Republic Senate Building" /> Even after its fall into disuse, many citizens considered the Senate Building a valuable landmark. In 3272 [[Lothal Calendar|LY]], Imperial inspectors reported that the Senate site attracted criminal activity, and discussion arose as to whether the building should be razed. The [[HoloNet News]] anchorman and Imperial propagandist [[Alton Kastle]] argued that the Senate Building should indeed be destroyed, as it harkened back to "less prosperous" times when the Empire was not in charge.<ref name="HoloNet News" />

Shortly after the fifteenth [[Empire Day|anniversary]] of the Imperial regime, the Senate Building was used to house a trap set for the [[Spectres|rebel crew]] of the ''[[Ghost]]''. [[Gall Trayvis]], a former [[Senator]] who posed as an Imperial dissident to trick rebel forces across [[the galaxy]], sent a transmission stating he would meet the crew in the Senate Building. When they arrived, they were confronted by [[Agent]] [[Alexsandr Kallus|Kallus]] of the [[Imperial Security Bureau]] as well as a squadron of [[stormtrooper]]s. The trap failed, however, as the rebels were able to escape.<ref name="Vision of Hope" />

